        id: 'quality-e2e-playwright-cypress', difficulty: 'senior', tags: ['e2e', 'playwright', 'cypress'],
        q: 'How do end-to-end tests with Playwright or Cypress fit into your testing strategy?',
        testing: 'Choosing the right level of test for each risk.',
        answer: `End-to-end tests run the real application in a browser and verify complete user journeys, such as signing in, changing a plan or paying a bill. They give the highest confidence but are slower and more fragile, so keep them few and focused on critical paths, with unit and component tests covering details. Use stable selectors, wait on conditions automatically, isolate test data and run them against a deployed or preview environment in CI, with traces, screenshots or videos kept for failures. Playwright supports several browsers and parallel runs and Cypress offers an interactive runner. For micro-frontends, run a small suite against the assembled application.`,
