        id: 'quality-eslint-prettier-flat-config', difficulty: 'senior', tags: ['eslint', 'prettier', 'typescript-eslint'],
        q: 'How do you set up ESLint and Prettier for a Vue 3 and TypeScript project?',
        testing: 'Linting and formatting responsibilities, and modern configuration.',
        answer: `ESLint checks code quality and potential errors, and Prettier only formats, so they have separate roles. Use <code>eslint-plugin-vue</code> with a recommended Vue 3 ruleset and <code>typescript-eslint</code> for TypeScript, and add <code>eslint-config-prettier</code> to turn off rules that conflict with the formatter. Current ESLint versions use a flat configuration file, <code>eslint.config.js</code>, where you compose configuration objects. Run lint with a zero-warning policy in CI, apply auto-fix locally and configure the editor to format on save. Keep the rules agreed by the team, and document any deliberate exceptions.`,
