        id: 'quality-husky-lint-staged-hooks', difficulty: 'foundation', tags: ['husky', 'lint-staged', 'git-hooks'],
        q: 'What are Husky and lint-staged, and why must CI still check the same things?',
        testing: 'Local quality gates and their limits.',
        answer: `Husky manages Git hooks in the repository, so checks run on events such as commit or push. lint-staged runs commands only on the files staged for commit, keeping the hook fast, for example lint and format on changed files. A common setup is a pre-commit hook for lint-staged, a commit-msg hook for commit message rules and sometimes a pre-push hook for tests. Hooks give fast feedback, but they can be skipped with a flag or may not be installed, so the pipeline must run the same checks as the authoritative gate. Keep hooks quick, or developers will bypass them.`,
