        q: 'Why does a Vite build not catch type errors, and how do you add type checking?',
        testing: 'Understanding the transpile-only behavior of the build.',
        answer: `Vite transpiles TypeScript with esbuild, which removes types without checking them, so a project with type errors can still build and run. Add a separate step that runs the type checker, which for Vue single-file components is <code>vue-tsc --noEmit</code>, and make it part of the build script or a dedicated pipeline stage. Run it in the editor for fast feedback and in CI as a required check. Keep the strict compiler options on, and treat a type error as a failing build.`,
