        id: 'quality-ci-pipeline-stages', difficulty: 'senior', tags: ['ci', 'pipeline', 'stages'],
        q: 'Describe the stages of a good CI pipeline for a frontend application.',
        testing: 'A complete and ordered pipeline with fast feedback.',
        answer: `A typical order: checkout, install dependencies with <code>npm ci</code> using a cache, lint, type check, unit and component tests with coverage, static analysis such as the Sonar scan with a quality gate, dependency audit, production build and an artifact that is stored. Then run end-to-end tests against a preview or test environment and, on the main branch, deploy to the next environment with smoke tests. Run independent stages in parallel and fail fast, so feedback arrives quickly. Make every check required for merging, keep the pipeline reproducible, with pinned Node and tool versions, and keep logs and reports available for diagnosis.`,
