        answer: `Keep secrets in the CI secret store or a vault, inject them only into the jobs that need them, mask them in logs and give them the least privilege. Never commit them, and prefer short-lived credentials from the platform where available. Rotate a secret that may have leaked. Protect the main branch: require pull requests, reviews and passing status checks such as lint, tests and the quality gate before merging, disallow force pushes and restrict who can approve production deployments. Remember that frontend build variables become public in the bundle, so real secrets must stay on the server.`,
