        q: 'How does the CI/CD pipeline work for Module Federation remotes in a micro-frontend system?',
        testing: 'Independent pipelines with safe integration.',
        answer: `<strong>Adapt this to your setup.</strong> Each remote has its own pipeline: install, lint, type check, tests with coverage, Sonar quality gate and a production build that emits hashed assets and the remote entry. The artifacts are published to a CDN or storage under a versioned path, and the host discovers the new version through a manifest or configuration that is updated only after contract and smoke tests pass. Release gradually with a canary or flag, monitor errors tagged by remote and version, and roll back by pointing the manifest to the previous version. Keep the remote entry cache short and keep old chunks available. A small end-to-end suite runs against the assembled shell and remotes.`,
