        q: 'Walk me through the build, test and deployment pipeline of your project.',
        testing: 'Real ownership of the delivery process.',
        answer: `<strong>Sample script, replace the brackets:</strong> "When a developer opens a pull request, the pipeline in GitLab CI installs dependencies with a cache, runs ESLint and the type check, then unit and component tests with [Vitest or Jest] and coverage. The Sonar scan imports the lcov report and the quality gate must pass for the new code. A build job creates the production bundle for the Self-care application and its Module Federation remotes and stores them as artifacts. After review and merge, the pipeline deploys to [dev, test, staging] and runs smoke and end-to-end tests, then promotes the same build to production after approval, with the manifest updated and a rollback option. Errors and performance are monitored by application and version."<br><br>Use the real stages, tools and numbers, such as pipeline duration, and say what you improved.`,
        mistake: 'Describing a generic pipeline that does not match what you actually operate, which is exposed by follow-up questions.',
        followupQ: 'What would you improve in this pipeline?',
        followupA: 'Give a concrete improvement such as caching, parallelization, better contract tests, quicker rollback or clearer ownership of failing builds.',
