        testing: 'Version control basics that cause real upgrade incidents.',
        answer: `A version has the form major.minor.patch. A patch is for backward-compatible fixes, a minor for backward-compatible features and a major for breaking changes. The caret <code>^1.2.3</code> allows updates that do not change the leftmost non-zero number, so minor and patch updates, and the tilde <code>~1.2.3</code> allows only patch updates. An exact version allows no automatic changes. For zero major versions, caret is stricter, because <code>^0.2.3</code> allows only patch changes. Ranges are resolved when installing, and the lockfile records the exact versions used, so ranges alone do not guarantee identical builds. Not every package follows semver perfectly, so test after upgrades.`,
