        answer: `Share a versioned design system and design tokens as the common foundation, ideally as CSS custom properties and a component package, so every application looks the same without copying styles. Prevent collisions with scoped styles, CSS modules or a naming prefix per application, and avoid global selectors and resets that leak. Shadow DOM gives strong isolation but complicates theming and global styles. Decide how component library versions are shared: a single shared version reduces drift, while per-application versions allow independent upgrades with some visual inconsistency. Test visually across applications and watch the CSS payload for duplication.`,
