        answer: `<strong>Sample script:</strong> "The project is a telecom platform. <strong>Self-care</strong> is the customer-facing website, built with Module Federation, where customers [for example view usage, change plans, pay bills, manage services]. <strong>Agent</strong> is used by support and sales agents to [for example look up a customer, handle requests, activate services, resolve issues], and it is hosted inside Salesforce. <strong>Retail</strong> is used in stores to [for example onboard customers, sell products, process orders]. Each domain has different users, permissions, performance expectations and release needs, so we built them as separate micro-frontends with a shared shell and common design system. They talk to backend services through [REST APIs or a gateway]. My responsibility was [your modules and tasks]."<br><br>Replace the examples with what the applications really do, and mention the scale you actually know.`,
        mistake: 'Describing screens without explaining who uses them and why they differ between domains.',
        followupQ: 'What differs most between the Self-care and Agent applications?',
