        testing: 'A structured description from shell to domain applications and shared services.',
        answer: `<strong>Sample script:</strong> "There is a shell application that handles the top-level routing, authentication, layout and loading of the micro-frontends. Each domain, Self-care, Agent and Retail, is a separate Vue application built and deployed independently by its own pipeline. [Self-care loads its remotes at runtime with Module Federation; say how the other domains are integrated.] Vue, Vue Router and Pinia are shared as singletons to avoid duplicates. A shared design system provides components and tokens, and shared packages provide authentication, API clients and utilities. Applications communicate through [events or a small shared context] with documented contracts. The Agent application is embedded in Salesforce through [your embedding method], which affects authentication, routing and styling. Deployment goes through CI/CD to a CDN, with a manifest that points to the live version of each application."<br><br>Draw it if possible: shell, three domains, shared libraries, backend, CDN and the Salesforce host.`,
        mistake: 'Giving a list of tools with no explanation of how loading, routing, sharing and deployment actually work.',
