        q: 'Explain the architecture of your project.',
        testing: 'Understanding of how the frontend is structured and how data flows, in your own words.',
        answer: `Describe it top to bottom: user interface, components, state and services, API layer and backend. Draw it if a whiteboard is available.<br><br><strong>Sample script:</strong> "It is a single-page application built with <code>Vue 3</code>. The folder structure is organized by feature, for example <code>features/orders</code>, with shared components, composables and utilities in common folders. Pages are lazy-loaded through the router. Components are small and reusable, and shared logic lives in composables. Server data goes through an API service layer built on <code>Axios</code> or <code>fetch</code>, with interceptors for authentication tokens and error handling. Shared client state, such as the logged-in user or filters, is kept in <code>Pinia</code> stores, while local UI state stays in the component. Forms use [validation library], and styling follows a design system built with <code>Tailwind CSS</code>. The app is built with <code>Vite</code> and deployed through a CI/CD pipeline that runs linting, tests and a build before release."<br><br>Be ready to explain why each choice was made and what you would change.`,
