        q: 'How does data flow in your application, from the API to the screen?',
        testing: 'Tracing a request through the layers and handling loading, error and update states.',
        answer: `Trace one real feature, for example a list page, end to end.<br><br><strong>Sample script:</strong> "When the user opens the orders page, the route component calls a composable such as <code>useOrders</code>. It calls the API service, which sends the request with the auth token added by an interceptor. While waiting, the page shows a loading state. When the response arrives I map it to the shape the UI needs and store it in a <code>Pinia</code> store if other pages share it, or in local state if only this page needs it. The component renders from that state. Errors are caught in the service or composable, mapped to a friendly message and shown with a retry option. When the user edits an item, we send the update, then either update the local state or refetch, and show a success or failure message."<br><br>Mention caching, pagination, debouncing and request cancellation if you used them.`,
