        testing: 'Clear ownership of work, from development to collaboration, without exaggeration.',
        answer: `Group your responsibilities into development, quality, collaboration and growth. Include only what you really do.<br><br><strong>Sample script:</strong> "As a [Frontend Developer or Senior Frontend Developer], my responsibilities are:<br>1. Developing features in <code>Vue 3</code> and <code>TypeScript</code> from designs and user stories.<br>2. Building reusable components and keeping them consistent with the design system.<br>3. Integrating REST APIs and handling loading, error and edge cases.<br>4. Writing unit and component tests, and fixing bugs raised by QA or from production.<br>5. Reviewing teammates' pull requests and giving feedback.<br>6. Improving performance, accessibility and browser compatibility.<br>7. Joining planning, refinement and daily stand-up meetings, and estimating tasks.<br>8. Working with designers, backend developers and QA to clarify requirements and unblock work.<br>9. [If true] Mentoring junior developers and helping with onboarding."<br><br>Use real examples for two or three of these points.`,
