        answer: `Use the STAR structure: situation, task, action, result. Choose a real problem you personally worked on.<br><br><strong>Sample script:</strong> "In [project], [situation, for example the product list page became very slow with large data]. My task was to [make it usable and under a target time]. I started by measuring with the browser performance tools and found [cause, such as rendering thousands of rows and repeated API calls]. I fixed it by [actions, such as pagination or virtual scrolling, debouncing search, caching responses and removing unnecessary re-renders]. As a result, [measurable outcome, for example load time dropped from X to Y or users stopped reporting freezes]. I also documented it and added a check so it would not return."<br><br>Other good topics: a hard bug, a migration, a tricky requirement or a conflict that you resolved.`,
