        q: 'Which checks belong before deployment versus after deployment?',
        testing: 'Layered release evidence and failure containment.',
        answer: `Before deployment, run deterministic linting, type checks, targeted tests and a production-build smoke suite, then verify artifact integrity and required configuration. Include critical browser journeys and dependency checks according to risk. After deployment, validate the actual serving path, headers, deep links, telemetry and essential transactions with safe test identities or read-only probes. Staging cannot fully prove production CDN or permission behavior. Keep checks fast enough to remain trusted, assign owners to failures and avoid routinely bypassing noisy gates. Pair both layers with a rehearsed rollback rather than treating passing CI as certainty.`,
