        answer: `Define a small number of critical journeys with clear start, success and failure conditions, such as loading an order and confirming a save. Measure completion and latency by release and coarse device or browser cohort, alongside errors. Distinguish abandonment from a known application failure and document measurement gaps. Set service objectives that reflect user harm and alert on sustained budget consumption, not every isolated exception. A page can produce no JavaScript errors while silently blocking submissions, so combine technical telemetry with task-level evidence and a safe synthetic check.`,
