        answer: `A lab run is a controlled observation with a particular device model, network, cache state and scripted interaction. Real sessions include weak hardware, extensions, long-lived tabs, varied content and third-party delays. Collect field metrics with supported APIs or a maintained measurement library, then compare distributions for meaningful cohorts rather than only global averages. Use lab traces to investigate a representative field problem and reproduce its journey. Sampling and consent affect who is observed, so state those limits. Neither a single Lighthouse score nor an aggregate percentile explains the causal bottleneck alone.`,
