        answer: `Identify the affected interaction and cohort, then separate time waiting for the main thread, event-handler execution and the delay before the next presentation. A slow click may be blocked by unrelated hydration work, expensive synchronous filtering or a layout-heavy update after a short handler. Capture privacy-safe attribution and reproduce under representative CPU conditions with a performance trace. Change the measured cause, such as splitting computation or reducing rendered work, then compare field cohorts after rollout. Avoid moving the same blocking work into a microtask because that still runs before the browser can paint.`,
