        answer: `Start with an allowlist of structured fields such as release, route template, error category and coarse timing. Strip query parameters, authorization headers, form values and document content before transmission. Treat screenshots, replay and free-form logs as especially sensitive, and do not enable them by default. Define lawful consent or another applicable basis, retention and access controls with the responsible privacy stakeholders. Sample deliberately and test redaction with representative sensitive fixtures. Server-side scrubbing is useful defense in depth, but avoiding collection is safer than hoping every later processor removes secrets correctly.`,
