        testing: 'Secure symbolication and artifact matching.',
        answer: `Generate source maps in a controlled build and associate them with the exact artifact and release identifier. Upload or retain them in a restricted symbolication system, then exclude map files from public serving when public source disclosure is not intended. Hidden map references alone do not make uploaded files private. Check whether maps embed source content and ensure no secrets entered the source in the first place. Verify a known stack against the deployed artifact and restrict access and retention. Incorrectly matched maps can produce convincing but false investigation evidence.`,
