        q: 'How can a browser error be correlated with backend work without creating unbounded telemetry?',
        testing: 'Trace context propagation with trust and cardinality boundaries.',
        answer: `Propagate a supported request or trace context only to approved origins and record a bounded correlation identifier on relevant failures. The server must treat incoming identifiers as untrusted metadata, not identity or authorization. Use route templates and error categories as metric dimensions; keep individual IDs in sampled logs or traces rather than metric labels. Apply length limits and sampling consistently, and verify CORS header implications where cross-origin tracing is intentional. This allows an engineer to follow one failed operation without turning every user or URL into a new time series.`,
