        answer: `Capture the release identity, affected journey, first observed time, approximate scope and representative sanitized failures. Record deployment and flag changes, plus whether server metrics indicate a shared dependency failure. Preserve a minimal reproduction or trace when quick, but do not delay an obvious safe rollback for perfect evidence. Maintain a timeline separating facts, hypotheses and actions, with one incident coordinator and clear updates. After mitigation, compare candidate and recovered cohorts and verify data integrity. This prevents a fortunate recovery from being mistaken for a proven root cause.`,
