        answer: `Telemetry should have bounded queues, payload size, retries and CPU overhead, and must not block rendering or core transactions. Batch low-priority events, drop expendable data under pressure and respect offline or consent state. A page-exit beacon is best effort, not guaranteed delivery. Handle endpoint errors without recursively reporting the reporting failure. Measure the collector's own impact and provide a kill switch for a faulty instrumentation release. Keep a small health signal for dropped events so an empty dashboard is not automatically interpreted as an error-free application.`,
