        answer: `Persist user intent with an operation ID, account scope, payload version and base resource revision. Replay only when authenticated under the same scope, and use server-supported idempotency because a lost response does not imply a failed write. Separate queued, sending, confirmed and conflicted states visibly. Apply bounded backoff and provide manual recovery when background synchronization is unavailable. Resolve conflicts according to the domain rather than overwriting silently. Never promise that a locally queued operation is already saved on the server; show its status and preserve a recoverable copy until confirmation.`,
