        testing: 'Separating notifications, exclusion and server-side correctness.',
        answer: `Use <code>BroadcastChannel</code> to announce invalidation or session changes, not as proof that only one tab owns a task. When available, Web Locks can serialize cooperating same-origin contexts, but tabs may close or suspend and support must be checked. Maintain server-side idempotency or session concurrency rules as the final correctness boundary. Include scope and version in messages, re-read authoritative state after notification and avoid broadcasting credentials. Provide a safe fallback when coordination APIs are unavailable. Test two actual contexts with delayed messages, termination and account changes, not just one tab twice.`,
