        answer: `State the problem and who is affected before proposing a solution, then list the constraints, options considered and why each was rejected or chosen. Include migration cost, compatibility, rollout and rollback, risks and open questions. Identify the affected teams and ask each for review explicitly, with a deadline and a named decision owner, so feedback does not drift indefinitely. Keep the document short enough to be read and use examples. Record the decision and its date, and link follow-up work. Treat dissent as information: address concerns directly, and if you proceed over an objection, document the reasoning and plan to check it later.`,
