        answer: `Identify a measurable cost such as repeated incident time, slow changes or abandonment caused by failures, then propose the smallest intervention likely to reduce it. Compare that option with doing nothing and with a larger rewrite, including delivery disruption and uncertainty. Set a checkpoint and outcome metric rather than promising vague future speed. A useful proposal explains which feature work becomes safer or cheaper and which risks remain. If the team intentionally defers the work, document the consequence and trigger for reconsideration instead of treating all debt as equally urgent.`,
