        q: 'What distinguishes a useful incident review from a blame-free meeting with no consequences?',
        testing: 'Systemic learning with owned, verifiable improvements.',
        answer: `Reconstruct the timeline and explain why the available information made the actions understandable, while still identifying decisions and controls that failed. Separate trigger, contributing conditions and impact. Choose a few corrective actions with owners, due dates and verification, such as a deployment gate or restore drill, rather than an exhaustive wishlist. Include what helped recovery and how communication worked. Blameless does not mean unaccountable: teams remain responsible for improving the system and following through. Review action effectiveness later instead of considering the incident closed when the document is written.`,
