        answer: `Define the coexistence boundary, supported combinations and an owner for both the migration and temporary adapters. Slice work into user-visible or independently verifiable areas that keep the product releasable. Track migrated usage, remaining dependency blockers and operational cost, not just completed pull requests. Establish explicit exit criteria and a budget for deleting compatibility code. A safe pause should leave a documented supported state, while resuming should not require rediscovering hidden assumptions. Resist combining unrelated redesigns with the migration because they expand rollback scope and obscure which change caused a regression.`,
