        testing: 'Loading strategy with loading and error states.',
        answer: `<code>defineAsyncComponent</code> takes a loader function that returns a dynamic import, so the component code is downloaded only when it is first rendered. It supports options for a loading component, an error component, a delay before showing the loading state and a timeout. Use it for heavy, below-the-fold or rarely used components such as charts and editors, and avoid it for content that must appear immediately. <code>Suspense</code> lets you show a fallback while async dependencies in a subtree, such as async setup or async components, resolve. Its API has been marked experimental in the documentation, so check the current status before relying on it in critical flows and always design the error path.`,
