        answer: `Deduplication coordinates overlapping executions for the same key; it is not a transaction and does not make a side-effecting handler safe. Nuxt versions expose policies such as cancel or defer, but the precise cancellation and signal behavior should be checked against the pinned release. Pass supported signals to abortable transport and keep handlers side-effect-free so retries or reruns cannot create duplicate writes. Return a defined serializable result to support payload reuse. Shared-key dedupe also does not replace correct identity dimensions or server idempotency. Test concurrent refreshes and confirm both visible state and actual transport behavior.`,
