        answer: `Give every control a real label, then connect its error text with <code>aria-describedby</code> and mark the invalid state with <code>aria-invalid</code>, so the message is read when the field is focused. State the problem and the fix in text, not only through a red border. On submit, show an error summary near the top with links to each field and move focus to it, so keyboard users do not have to hunt for failures. Avoid validating aggressively while the user is still typing, and avoid announcing every keystroke through a live region, which floods a screen reader. Preserve entered values and keep required hints visible before the error, not only after it. Test the complete flow with a keyboard and a screen reader, including recovery from an error.`,
