        answer: `Choose an actual personal situation, not a borrowed model anecdote. Explain what you believed, which information supported that view and what you personally owned. Describe the contradictory evidence and how you checked it rather than changing direction merely because someone more senior disagreed. Show how you communicated the reversal, limited sunk-cost thinking and helped the team recover. State the real outcome with accurate attribution; if no numeric measurement exists, describe observable evidence and its limits. Finish with the decision habit you changed. It is acceptable to say you lack an example at the requested scale.`,
