        answer: `Measure first. Show the widget's share of main-thread time and its effect on interaction latency using field data segmented by pages and devices, so the discussion rests on numbers. Then offer options that preserve the business goal: load it after the page is interactive or on user intent such as hover or click, use a lightweight facade until needed, restrict it to the pages where it earns its value, and move work off the main thread where the vendor supports it. Set a performance budget for third-party code and review it regularly. Present the cost and benefit together so the decision to keep it is informed.`,
        diagnosis: 'Profile long tasks attributed to the vendor script, and compare interaction metrics for sessions with and without it. Identify when it loads and what it does on each page.',
