        answer: `Reproduce on a real Safari or a faithful environment and capture the console error and failing code path. Common causes are a newer API or CSS feature without support, differences in date parsing, stricter handling of storage or cookies, regex or lookbehind support, and layout differences such as viewport units. Check compatibility data for each API involved and the browserslist target used by the build. Fix with a supported alternative or a feature-detected fallback, not a user-agent check. Add Safari to the automated test matrix so the problem is caught before release.`,
